  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender Audit for the WASH and WRM projects in Afghanistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Roughly 61% of rural Afghans do not have access to safe drinking water. In Ghor Province in the central highlands, the percentage jumps to 92%, making it the worst ranked province in the country for clean drinking water. In Lal District, the eastern-most district of Ghor, CRS assessment data indicates that a lack of safe drinking water is a major issue for family health, with children experiencing diarrhoea as much as 2-3 times per month.   
 
The strong gender component , with sex disaggregated data included in baseline and reporting data, and with women&apos;s empowerment element in the WASH work, contributes to the gender priority within our partner international  programme priorities. In addition, a gender audit will be undertaken by CAFOD and the development of a plan to address recommendations will improve CRS, our partner Afghanistan&apos;s capacity to engage in gender equitable and responsive practices and programming</narrative>
  </description>
